    "korean_title": "Tier4 Nebula v1.3.0 릴리스 - Hesai 센서 타임스탬프 버그 수정",
    "korean_summary": "Nebula 라이브러리가 Hesai 스캔의 제로 타임스탬프 버그를 수정하고 Agnocast 2.4.0 의존성을 업그레이드했다."
   },
   "summary_data": null,
   "related": [],
   "uid": "gh:tier4/nebula:v1.3.0",
   "body": "This release fixes Hesai scans being published with a zero timestamp when the decoder starts outside the configured FoV, and brings Nebula's Agnocast wrapper in line with autoware_core, adding <autoware_node> launch support. Upgrading This release requires agnocast 2.4.0 (up from 2.3.5). Workspaces building with ENABLE_AGNOCAST=1 must re-import build_depends-humble.repos before building. Hesai scans that previously reached the pointcloud publisher with a zero timestamp — a partial scan emitted when the decoder initialised, or was rebuilt during replay, while the sensor azimuth lay outside the configured FoV — are now dropped rather than published. Downstream consumers that saw the resulting zeroed concatenated clouds will no longer receive them. What's Changed fix(nebula_hesai_decoders): drop scans whose timestamp was never set by @ogrex in #493 chore: sync files by @tier4-nebula-app[bot] in #483 fix(nebula_core_ros): build the synced agnocast_wrapper Node implementation by @Koichi98 in #494 chore(nebula_core_ros): follow upstream's agnocast_wrapper layout by @Koichi98 in #495 chore(nebula_core_ros): sync agnocast_wrapper from autoware_core by @Koichi98 in #496 chore: release v1.3.0 by @drwnz in #497 New Contributors @ogrex made their first contribution in #493 Full Changelog : v1.2.0...v1.3.0"
  }
 ],
